<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Shō dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1406">1406</a>–<a href="/years/1469">1469</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as First Sho dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Shō dynasty ruled the kingdom of Chūzan and then a unified Ryukyu from 1406 to 1469. It was founded when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-hashi">Shō Hashi</a> installed his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-shisho">Shō Shishō</a> as king, and it completed the unification of Okinawa in 1429. After Shō Hashi's death a series of short reigns and internal conflicts weakened it, and on the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-toku">Shō Toku</a> the treasurer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-en">Kanemaru</a> took power as Shō En.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-sho-dynasty.jpg" alt="First Shō dynasty" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 663highland · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naha_Shuri_Castle51s3s4200.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
